hello and welcome to the agenda  next week we'll be in strasbourg for the  last plenary before christmas  let's take a look at what's on offer  first up president jean-claude juncker  will present the commission's priorities  for 2015.  last time around the plenary he unveiled  a 315 billion euro investment plan for  europe  citizens businesses have all been  calling for change  for a refocus on jobs and growth but how  can europe begin its rejuvenation over  the coming years  on which programs will money be spent  we'll find out on tuesday  priorities are all well and good but the  eu  has some big bills to pay and that's  been a sticking point for signing off on  next year's budget  once again here we are at the end of the  year and the budget is up in the air  a preliminary deal has now been reached  between eu leaders and the parliament on  a condition  that the commission starts to pay off  unpaid bills totaling 23.5 billion euros  and get debts under control by 2016.  on wednesday it'll be d-day for the  141.2 billion euros  2015 budget find out how the vote goes  at the plenary  could a landmark vote by the european  parliament to recognize the state of  palestine be the catalyst to address the  palestinian question  in a move that angered israel sweden  became the first western european member  state to officially recognize palestine  in october  the uk spain and ireland have all held  symbolic votes with france and possibly  also belgium  set to follow suit will the non-binding  resolution get the support it needs  find out on wednesday how to find the  right balance between the respective  life  and border security meps will debate  migration in the mediterranean  on wednesday also look out for a vote on  the european ombudsman  a vote will take place to elect the  incumbent emily o'reilly on tuesday  but possibly one of the big highlights  of the last session before christmas  will be the unveiling of the winner  of the lux film prize 2014. here at the  parliament and across member states  screenings have been taking place for  all three films which one wins  france's girlhood by celine skiema  polish director  pavel pavlakovsky's eda or how about the  last finalist slovenian class  enemy by rock beach i guess we'll have  to wait to find out  and that's all we have for this agenda  take care and enjoy the week
 

